     {
      "id": "6adf1c2efd1c47893ffc0b9a",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Click Through Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a click through landing page?\", \"a\": \"A click through landing page explains one offer, then hands the visitor to another page to buy or sign up. Unbounce describes it as having a simple button as the call to action that sends the visitor into the checkout flow, where a lead gen page would have a form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a click through landing page?\", \"a\": \"Decide where the button goes and what its link should carry, such as the chosen plan or the item for the cart. Then describe the offer and its destination to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, which builds the page and a log of every click. Press the button on a phone before any traffic arrives.\"}, {\"q\": \"How is a click through landing page different from one with a signup form?\", \"a\": \"The difference is where the visitor acts. A click through page has no form of its own: its button opens another page, and the signup or purchase happens there. Unbounce says lead gen pages, which it also calls squeeze pages, use a form as their call to action, and that form collects the details on the page itself.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where should the button go on a click through landing page?\", \"a\": \"Put the first button right after the section that answers the visitor's main question, then repeat the same button lower down with the same label and destination. On a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/mobile'>mobile landing page</a>, keep one button on screen without scrolling and make it wide enough to press with a thumb.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a click through landing page pass to the checkout page?\", \"a\": \"Pass whatever the visitor has already chosen on the page: the tier they clicked, the product and how many, any discount code. On a Shopify store, a cart permalink that sends the customer to a checkout with the selected merchandise is the default, and the same link creates a new checkout for each customer.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I track which campaign a click through landing page visitor came from?\", \"a\": \"Log each button click with the campaign tags the visitor arrived with, then match those tags against the signups on the next page. Compare the two per campaign each week. An app built with Emergent keeps that click log in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a click through landing page include a video?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A short demo above the button can show what a screenshot cannot, as long as the button sits beside it and does not wait for the video to end. A page built around the video itself is a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/video'>video landing page</a>, which has its own layout and playback choices.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a click through landing page show the price before checkout?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when the next page asks for payment. A visitor who meets the price for the first time at checkout has to decide all over again, while one who read it on the page has already decided. For a free trial, say what happens to the account when the trial ends.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a click through landing page send visitors to a free trial?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Unbounce counts signup landing pages as one form of click through page. They ask visitors to take a first step by signing up for a free trial or subscription. Carry the chosen plan into the signup link so the visitor does not pick it twice.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a click through landing page work from a printed flyer?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Print a QR code that opens the page, and give that link its own utm_campaign value so scans show up apart from email visits. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/qr-code'>qr code landing page</a> covers the scan side in more depth. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6adb17f75753424908a700fc",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Interactive Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an interactive landing page?\", \"a\": \"An interactive landing page is a single-goal page where the visitor operates something, such as a price calculator or a product quiz, and gets a result back on the same screen. What they enter is saved with their contact details, which tells sales what each prospect asked about.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an interactive landing page?\", \"a\": \"Write down the inputs, the formula or quiz logic, and where the result appears. Then describe that to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, which builds it with the calculator or quiz included. Check several results against your own math and tab through every field before you publish.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do good interactive landing page examples ask visitors to do?\", \"a\": \"They ask for something the visitor can answer without looking it up, such as an office size or how they brew coffee, and they return a result at once. When you study an example, count its inputs and note whether the result comes before the form or after it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is an interactive landing page the same as an animated one?\", \"a\": \"No. An interactive page changes because the visitor did something, such as typing a number or picking an answer. An <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/animated'>animated landing page</a> moves on its own as it loads or scrolls. One page can do both, and a quiz with no motion at all is still interactive.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should an interactive landing page show the result before asking for an email?\", \"a\": \"Yes, show the result first. Once visitors know the number, an email field reads as a way to keep it; placed in front of the answer, it asks for trust before the number has proven useful. Put the form directly under the result, with the inputs carried over.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should a quiz on an interactive landing page have?\", \"a\": \"Start with 4, and add a question only when it changes the result. If every answer to a question leads to the same recommendation, cut it. Show progress, such as question 2 of 4, and when the quiz needs another question later, add it by prompting Emergent again.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a printed flyer link to an interactive landing page?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Point a QR code at the page URL, and the visitor lands on the calculator or quiz with nothing to type. Because the scan happens on a phone, treat the page as a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/qr-code'>qr code landing page</a>: one control that fits the screen and a button large enough for a thumb.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make an interactive landing page work with a keyboard?\", \"a\": \"Use real form controls for every input and test the page with the Tab key. WCAG 2.1.1 asks that all functionality of the content is operable through a keyboard interface. Put the result in an output element: MDN notes that assistive technology will announce the results of UI interactions posted inside it without requiring that focus is switched away from the controls.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an interactive landing page save from each visitor?\", \"a\": \"Save every input next to the contact details, plus the result the page showed. A lead that reads 4,000 square feet, 12 visits, and $1,440 a month tells sales the quote before the first call. In the app Emergent builds, that data lives in a database the business owns and can sync to any tool with an API.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do the sliders on an interactive landing page work on a phone?\", \"a\": \"They can, if each one is sized for a thumb and paired with a number field for an exact value. Set that field's inputmode attribute to numeric, which MDN describes as a numeric input keyboard that only requires the digits. Then test on a real phone: on a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/mobile'>mobile landing page</a>, keep the result on the same screen as the inputs.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6adf1ae6aa57742b4bc9aea7",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Minimalist Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a minimalist landing page?\", \"a\": \"A minimalist landing page is a single page built around one offer and one next step, with every other part taken out. NN/g describes minimalist design as an approach that seeks to simplify interfaces by removing unnecessary elements or content that does not support user tasks. On a landing page, that task is the one button or form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a minimalist landing page?\", \"a\": \"Decide the sentence the page must say and the thing a visitor should do, then cut every part that serves neither. Describe those choices and your typeface to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>. It builds the page with a database for the entries, and you adjust spacing or copy by prompting again.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a minimalist landing page include?\", \"a\": \"A headline that states the offer, a line or two of support, one image or none, and one button or form. Add proof only where a visitor needs it to act, such as a price or a delivery time. On a page Emergent builds, that form saves each entry to a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does a minimalist landing page work for people who scan a code on a poster?\", \"a\": \"Yes, as long as the headline repeats the poster's offer word for word. A visitor who scans a printed code arrives on a phone. Put the headline and the button on the first screen and leave out anything that needs scrolling. The <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/qr-code'>qr code landing page</a> guide covers the code itself and where to print it.\"}, {\"q\": \"How much white space should a minimalist landing page have?\", \"a\": \"Enough that the headline and the button each read on their own at a glance. A practical start is to leave space above and below the headline at least as tall as the headline itself. Keep the same clearance around the button, then judge the result on a phone, where the screen is narrowest.\"}, {\"q\": \"What colors work on a minimalist landing page?\", \"a\": \"Start with a neutral background, one text color, and one accent that only the button uses. Then check each pair against WCAG 2.2: large-scale text, such as a big headline, can pass at 3:1, while body copy needs 4.5:1 or more.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I keep a minimalist landing page readable on a phone?\", \"a\": \"Test it on a real phone, not a resized browser window. Body text should read without zooming, the headline should wrap without leaving one word alone on a line, and the button should be wide enough for a thumb. The <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/mobile'>mobile landing page</a> guide covers phone layouts in more detail.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do I need a template to build a minimalist landing page?\", \"a\": \"No. Emergent builds the page from a plain-English prompt and changes it by prompting. You start from your own message instead of someone else's sections. On paid plans, the full code exports to your GitHub repository, where you or a developer can edit it directly.\"}, {\"q\": \"What fonts suit a minimalist landing page?\", \"a\": \"A serif or a sans serif both work, as long as the headline is set large and heavy and the body face stays clear at small sizes. NN/g notes that bold or large typography becomes another tool for communicating meaning when there are few elements on the page. To swap the face later, prompt Emergent with the new font name.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a minimalist landing page use motion?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if each motion is small and has a reason, such as a fade on the headline or a hover state on the button. Skip looping backgrounds, which put a second moving thing next to the one action. Pages built around motion are covered in the <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/animated'>animated landing page</a> guide.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6ad8624f9a7530b3764bdc33",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Portfolio Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a portfolio landing page?\", \"a\": \"A portfolio landing page is one page that shows a short selection of your best work and asks the visitor to take a single next step. That step might be asking about a date or opening a case study. A full portfolio site spreads the work over many pages; this page keeps the work and the one action together.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a portfolio landing page?\", \"a\": \"Write one prompt that names your projects and where each inquiry should go, and Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a> builds the page and the database behind it. Change a section later with another prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do strong landing page portfolio examples have in common?\", \"a\": \"They lead with the work, before any introduction. Each project names the person's role and one result. Look for one clear action placed under the work it relates to, and a short list of projects rather than everything ever made. Borrow the structure of the examples you like, then fill it with your own work.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a portfolio landing page for company clients differ from one for individuals?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Expect a company client to forward the page to colleagues. Name the business problem each project solved, and add a way to reach you that does not need a phone call. If the page has to sell a service to a buying team rather than show your work, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/b2b'>b2b landing page</a> fits that job better.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I show client work under NDA on a portfolio landing page?\", \"a\": \"Ask the client first what you may show, and get the answer in writing. If the full case study cannot be public, show the project title and your role, and open the details only to a visitor who enters a work email. The app saves each of those visits as a row with the company name.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a portfolio landing page use an inquiry form or an email address?\", \"a\": \"Use a form when you need the same facts from everyone, such as a date or a budget. A bare email address leaves you to ask for those facts one reply at a time. An app Emergent builds saves each form entry to a database you own, and you can name the requests that should send you an alert.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a printed business card link to my portfolio landing page?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Print a QR code on the card that opens the page, and give it a link tagged for print so you can tell those visits from the rest. Test the code on two phones before the print run. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/qr-code'>qr code landing page</a> covers how to set up a page whose visitors arrive from a scan.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a web address at my name worth it for a portfolio landing page?\", \"a\": \"Yes: a short address such as yourname.com is easier to type from a resume and reads as yours. Emergent includes custom domains, which use credits, and the page can sit at your name from the day it goes up.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a developer's portfolio landing page add new projects on its own?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when the page reads your projects from the code host instead of from text you type. An app Emergent builds can pull data in from a service with an API on a schedule. Each new public project then gets its card without an edit to the page.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a portfolio landing page be the first step of a sales funnel?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The portfolio earns the inquiry, and the steps after it, such as a discovery call booking or a proposal, can live on their own pages. If you sell a fixed package rather than custom work, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/sales-funnel'>sales funnel landing page</a> is built around that sequence of steps.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6ad8624f9a7530b3764bdc37",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Service Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a service landing page?\", \"a\": \"A service landing page is a single web page that sells one service, such as a furnace repair or a lawn mowing plan, and asks the visitor to request it. It carries the offer, the area served, the price or how pricing works, and one form or call button, with nothing that leads away from the request.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a service landing page?\", \"a\": \"Pick the one service the page sells and list the ZIP codes you cover, then describe both to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, along with who should hear about each request. Emergent builds the page and the database behind it from that prompt, and you change the offer or the form later by prompting again.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a landing page for my service business ask visitors to do?\", \"a\": \"Ask for one thing: a request for the service the page sells, or a phone call. Match the action to how the job gets scheduled. A fixed-price visit can be booked straight from the form, while a job that needs an estimate should end in a request for one. Keep a second, competing button off the page.\"}, {\"q\": \"What makes the best landing page for a service business?\", \"a\": \"One job, one service area, and a plain next step make the best page: a price or an estimate, a short form, and a phone number. Write one page per service, not one for the whole company. A general <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/business'>business landing page</a> suits offers that are not a single job, such as wholesale orders or catering.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do the strongest landing page examples for services have in common?\", \"a\": \"Each of the four examples above sells one job and runs one rule behind its form: a ZIP code check, a price per visit, a route to the right person, or a cap on bookings per Saturday. When you study any service page, look for that rule first. It decides what happens after the visitor presses the button.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a tree service landing page include?\", \"a\": \"Include the jobs the crew does, such as removal, trimming, or stump grinding, as separate choices on the form, plus the ZIP codes you cover. Ask where the tree stands and whether it is near the house or power lines; the estimator needs both before the site visit. Photos of finished jobs from your own crew do more than stock images.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I write a service landing page that sells to other companies?\", \"a\": \"Name the business result in the headline, show the scope of the service and the kind of company it suits, and end with one request, such as a site visit or a call. Put the commercial details on the page too, like the hours your crews work and how you invoice. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/b2b'>b2b landing page</a> covers longer buying decisions with several people involved.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do I need a separate service landing page for each service I offer?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when you send ads or mailers to that service. A visitor who searched for gutter cleaning should see gutter cleaning first. Keep a combined services page on your main site for browsing. Emergent builds each page from its own prompt, and every page's requests land in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I track which ads bring requests to my service business landing page?\", \"a\": \"Give each ad its own link with a campaign tag, and add a hidden field to the form that saves that tag with the request. Count requests by tag each week and cut the ads that send none. Requests from a page Emergent builds are stored in a database you own, and each row carries the tag beside the request details.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I send people from a printed flyer to my service landing page?\", \"a\": \"Print a QR code and a short web address that open the page for the one service on the flyer, not your home page. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/qr-code'>qr code landing page</a> is read on a phone. Keep its first screen light: web.dev says sites should strive to have Largest Contentful Paint of 2.5 seconds or less. Repeat the offer from the print at the top.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6af709944a92a552531bb5d7",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Competitor Comparison FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What are competitor comparison landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Competitor comparison landing pages are pages on your own site that compare your product with one named rival, row by row. They answer a search for one product against the other, or for an alternative to the rival, with a table and one next step, such as a trial.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create competitor comparison landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Write down the search you want to answer, pick six to eight rows buyers decide on, and find the source for every rival claim. Then describe the page to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>. It builds the table and the form from your prompt, and each lead lands in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should the table on competitor comparison landing pages include?\", \"a\": \"The table should hold the rows a buyer decides on, each side's answer in plain words, and a source link under every rival cell. Add the date each rival cell was checked. Drop rows where both products match, unless buyers expect to see them.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I learn which features to compare on competitor comparison landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Ask them. Send a five-question survey to recent customers and to deals you lost, asking which tools they looked at and which difference decided it. A training software company could borrow from learning and development survey questions to hear how its buyers rank features. Emergent builds the survey from a prompt, with no response caps.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can competitor comparison landing pages name the rival brand they compare against?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The FTC's policy on comparative advertising encourages naming competitors, but requires clarity and, if necessary, disclosure to avoid deceiving the consumer. In practice, say what you compared and link the rival's own page for each claim. For anything beyond that, ask a lawyer.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make competitor comparison landing pages work on a phone?\", \"a\": \"Keep two columns on a phone: your product and one rival, with the row label above each pair of answers. Pin the column names to the top of the screen as the reader scrolls. Put a third rival behind a switch at the top instead of a sideways scroll.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which rival should I build competitor comparison landing pages against first?\", \"a\": \"Start with the rival your lost deals name first, because that page answers a question your buyers already ask. Check that people search the two names together before you write. A game studio can ask players which titles they also play with game survey questions, then compare against the one named first.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should competitor comparison landing pages be updated?\", \"a\": \"Recheck every rival cell on a fixed schedule, such as every 90 days, and again whenever a rival announces new pricing. Change the check date on the page each time. In an app Emergent builds, each check date sits in your own database, and the app can email the page owner when a cell passes its age.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should competitor comparison landing pages show the rival's prices?\", \"a\": \"Show a rival's price only when the rival publishes it, and link the public page with the date you read it. If the rival quotes prices on request, say that instead of guessing a number. A price you estimated is a claim you cannot back up.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do buyers want from competitor comparison landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Buyers on a comparison page already have a shortlist. They want the one difference that settles it, with proof they can open and check. To hear it from your own readers, send audience survey questions to your newsletter list before you write the rows.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     }
    ]
   }
